 "reconciliation": "SEVENTEEN of the seventeen columns this leaf carries a footing for close exactly, residual zero on every one - eight free white male, seven free white female, and the two free coloured figures. THE CLOSURE SETTLES THREE MARKS THE CROPS ALONE WOULD HAVE LEFT OPEN. Line 14's mark in m_30_40 is HOLLOW where every other 1 in that column is solid - a split nib, not a different figure - and m_30_40 closes at 16 only if it is a 1. Line 17's mark in m_10_15 and line 18's in f_5_10 are heavy blots with no legible form, and each column closes only if its blot is a 1. None of the three was read off the footing: each was read as a 1 from its own length and slant beside the solid 1s above it, and the footing then agreed. IT ALSO SEPARATES TWO FORMS OF THE HAND'S ALPHABET. Over m_u5 stand a diagonal and a small separate loop, and over f_30_40 stands one stroke whose loop closes at the top into a tail running down-left. The first is a 1 beside a 0 and reads 10; the second is a 9. The cells give 10 and 9 independently, and the two glyphs are not the same mark. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK IS NOT EMPTY AND IT IS ALL ONE HOUSEHOLD: two free coloured females, one under 10 and one of 24 to 36, both on line 19 in the household of Mrs. Nan[?]y H. Jackson, whose twenty-six free white cells are every one of them blank. The footing row carries those same two figures and nothing else in any of its twelve columns.",
